{"type":"tool_result","run_id":"run_f7c5db228f62","seq":17,"ts":"2026-10-30T11:56:36.630907Z","data":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b2016d298794a349ad19506660b64a8","name":"describe_phenotype","ok":true,"error":null,"evidence_id":"e4","kind":"phenotype","summary":"Microscopist on 4 field(s): density lower vs DMSO; 7 observations; candidates: Microtubule stabilizers","image_ids":["f_9b59e1d37c99.composite","f_16a87df931ce.composite","f_d07dbcbe0003.composite","f_d53528433533.composite","f_b165a4caad77.composite"],"data":{"field_ids":["f_9b59e1d37c99","f_16a87df931ce","f_d07dbcbe0003","f_d53528433533"],"dmso_field_ids":["f_b165a4caad77"],"model":"meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026","images":"composites only","report":{"cell_density":"lower","observations":[{"channel":"tubulin","finding":"green signal markedly brighter vs DMSO at identical contrast. Filamentous network replaced by intense bundles/rings/asters and bright foci on near-black background, high cell-to-cell and intra-cell variation and edge contrast.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"tubulin","finding":"Quantitative: increased mean intensity, increased intensity SD, increased GLCM contrast texture.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"actin","finding":"red cortical signal brighter vs DMSO, more heterogeneous and high-contrast. Rounded cells with strong peripheral red rim, dark gaps between cells more apparent due to loss of confluence.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"actin","finding":"Quantitative: increased mean intensity, increased intensity SD, increased GLCM contrast.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"dna","finding":"blue nuclei not uniformly oval as in DMSO. Outlines lobed/indented/irregular, some multilobed and condensed bright white-yellow mitotic-like masses where blue overlaps intense green/red. Less circular/compact.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"dna","finding":"Quantitative: decreased nuclear solidity 0.956 vs DMSO median 0.973 z=-25.7 and decreased form factor 0.849 vs 0.914 z=-15.8 = less solid, less circular nuclei.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"composite","finding":"All 4 treated fields consistent: sparse vs dense confluent epithelial monolayer in DMSO control f_b165a4caad77. Many rounded, isolated cells and small clumps; frequent bright yellow-white overlap indicating concurrent tubulin/actin/DNA condensation. Consistent with mitotic arrest/cytotoxicity at 0.3uM, 206 cells measured.","agrees_with_measurements":false}],"notable_cells":[{"field_id":"f_9b59e1d37c99","x":450,"y":320,"why":"distinct bright green ring/bundle structures"},{"field_id":"f_d53528433533","x":400,"y":500,"why":"multiple rounded yellow mitotic-like cells with high tubulin intensity"}],"candidate_mechanisms":[{"moa":"Microtubule stabilizers","why":"massive positive z tub_mean 46.0, tub_std 74.7, tub_glcm_contrast 65.5 with visibly brighter bundled tubulin indicates increased polymerization/bundling. Destabilizers would decrease tub_mean. Accompanied by reduced solidity/form factor and increased act heterogeneity secondary to rounding/mitotic arrest. Visible only as composite 1024x819 px, color-assigned, so inferred from green vs red vs blue at identical contrast."}],"uncertainty":"Only composites provided. No grayscale channels to separate stains unambiguously, but DMSO vs treated contrast identical so intensity increases are real. No z-scores provided for cell count; density loss noted visually but set agrees=false as not covered."}},"cost_usd":0.02103}}
