{"type":"tool_result","run_id":"run_f7c5db228f62","seq":20,"ts":"2026-10-30T11:56:59.152668Z","data":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-7e1145254f074107b6a10b6c9a52b8ae","name":"describe_phenotype","ok":true,"error":null,"evidence_id":"e5","kind":"phenotype","summary":"Microscopist on 4 field(s): density lower vs DMSO; 6 observations; candidates: Microtubule stabilizers","image_ids":["f_136d4ffe180f.composite","f_606ce44cd339.composite","f_0abcbb5b473e.composite","f_0c227b3ae2ec.composite","f_b165a4caad77.composite"],"data":{"field_ids":["f_136d4ffe180f","f_606ce44cd339","f_0abcbb5b473e","f_0c227b3ae2ec"],"dmso_field_ids":["f_b165a4caad77"],"model":"meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026","images":"composites only","report":{"cell_density":"lower","observations":[{"channel":"composite","finding":"Treated fields 4/4 show markedly lower confluence vs DMSO f_b165a4caad77. DMSO: dense monolayer ~200+ nuclei/field with overlapping cytoplasms. Treated: 30-60 cells/field, isolated or small clusters, large black background. Consistent with growth arrest / loss.","agrees_with_measurements":false},{"channel":"tubulin","finding":"Beta-tubulin (green in composite) is profoundly brighter, thicker and more heterogeneous in treated vs DMSO. DMSO: dim diffuse perinuclear network with fine radiating microtubules. Treated: intense thick bundles, hollow rings, aster-like and crescent arrays filling rounded cells, high spatial contrast and patchiness. Many cells show saturated yellow-green where tubulin dominates.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"tubulin","finding":"Quantitatively this is a strong increase in tubulin intensity and texture. No separate grayscale given, but green channel intensity and variance clearly elevated.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"actin","finding":"F-actin (red in composite) also brighter and reorganized. DMSO: thin cortical actin, stress fibers. Treated: broad, spiky peripheral lamellae/ruffles, red rim around enlarged rounded cells, plus diffuse increase in red signal co-localizing with tubulin bundles.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"dna","finding":"DNA (blue in composite, faint in these composites) nuclei are larger, irregular, lobed and less circular vs round-oval DMSO nuclei. Reduced solidity/form factor visible as notched, kidney-shaped or fragmented outlines, often obscured by bright green/red but still blue-purple when visible; mitotic condensed chromosomes appear as bright yellow (blue+green+red overlap) spheres.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"dna","finding":"Increased multinucleation/micronucleation. DMSO: predominantly 1 nucleus/cell. Treated: frequent cells with 2-6 closely apposed nuclei or micronuclei and clusters of yellow condensed nuclei (e.g., f_136d4ffe180f bottom-left 8-nucleus cluster, f_0c227b3ae2ec bottom-left 5-nucleus chain; large multinucleate cells in f_606ce44cd339 lower-right).","agrees_with_measurements":true}],"notable_cells":[{"field_id":"f_136d4ffe180f","x":820,"y":560,"why":"Large flat cell with dense microtubule aster bundles and lobed nucleus illustrating tub_mean/std increase"},{"field_id":"f_606ce44cd339","x":175,"y":295,"why":"Enlarged rounded cell with thick green ring/crescent microtubule bundle and spiky red actin rim, typical of stabilizer phenotype"},{"field_id":"f_0c227b3ae2ec","x":198,"y":760,"why":"Multinucleate cluster with 5 bright yellow condensed nuclei in shared cytoplasm"}],"candidate_mechanisms":[{"moa":"Microtubule stabilizers","why":"Best matches composite: massive tub_mean z=42.8, tub_std z=75.1, tub_glcm_contrast z=59.5 - visible as hyper-intense, thick, high-contrast microtubule bundles, asters and rings in rounded arrested cells, with increased act_mean z=41.3/act_std z=17.9 secondary to rounding/spreading and frequent multinucleation frac_multinucleate_proxy z=13.6 plus reduced nuc_solidity z=-33.3 / nuc_form_factor z=-18.2 visible as lobed irregular nuclei. This pattern is classic for taxane-like stabilization, not destabilization (which decreases tubulin signal), actin disruption (which decreases actin), or Aurora/Eg5 alone."}],"uncertainty":"DNA channel read from blue in composite only, no grayscale; DAPI intensity not in top deviations. Other list members (Aurora kinase inhibitors, Eg5 inhibitors) also produce multinucleation but do not produce this extreme tubulin hyper-intensity/texture, so excluded. No evidence for Cholesterol-lowering, DNA damage/replication, Kinase inhibitors, Protein degradation/synthesis or Epithelial from these images alone."}},"cost_usd":0.01921}}
